{"event_id":"EVT-000079","timestamp_utc":"2026-08-12T15:16:21.583Z","session_id":"SESSION-BATCH-20260812T150310676130Z","run_id":"RUN-TRF-014-20260812T151130900147Z","requirement_id":"TRF-014","event_type":"iteration_completed","iteration":3,"static_valid":true,"validator_accept":false,"matcher_activated":false,"decision":"REVISE","feedback":"Remove the standalone constraint that requires exactly one firstScheduledDryDockingDate for every pre-1 July 2007 triggered ship; the regulation requires the marking by that event, not a dry-docking-date record, and an already correctly marked ship must not fail merely because that date is absent. Restructure the pre-2007 logic so an unmarked ship may defer the marking only when a valid first scheduled dry-docking date after 1 July 2007 is evidenced and has not yet arrived; if the marking is already complete and equals the certificate maximum amidships draught, permit conformance without dry-docking-date evidence, while ensuring missing date evidence cannot make an unmarked ship pass accidentally.","generator_elapsed_ms":77410.856,"validator_elapsed_ms":31923.599}
{"event_id":"EVT-000080","timestamp_utc":"2026-08-12T15:16:21.584Z","session_id":"SESSION-BATCH-20260812T150310676130Z","run_id":"RUN-TRF-014-20260812T151130900147Z","requirement_id":"TRF-014","event_type":"unresolved_issue","iteration":3,"issue_type":"MAX_ATTEMPTS_REACHED","detail":"Remove the standalone constraint that requires exactly one firstScheduledDryDockingDate for every pre-1 July 2007 triggered ship; the regulation requires the marking by that event, not a dry-docking-date record, and an already correctly marked ship must not fail merely because that date is absent. Restructure the pre-2007 logic so an unmarked ship may defer the marking only when a valid first scheduled dry-docking date after 1 July 2007 is evidenced and has not yet arrived; if the marking is already complete and equals the certificate maximum amidships draught, permit conformance without dry-docking-date evidence, while ensuring missing date evidence cannot make an unmarked ship pass accidentally.","status":"OPEN"}
{"event_id":"EVT-000081","timestamp_utc":"2026-08-12T15:16:21.584Z","session_id":"SESSION-BATCH-20260812T150310676130Z","run_id":"RUN-TRF-014-20260812T151130900147Z","requirement_id":"TRF-014","event_type":"run_finished","status":"MAX_ATTEMPTS_REACHED","accepted":false,"attempts":3,"final_shape":"","final_feedback":"Remove the standalone constraint that requires exactly one firstScheduledDryDockingDate for every pre-1 July 2007 triggered ship; the regulation requires the marking by that event, not a dry-docking-date record, and an already correctly marked ship must not fail merely because that date is absent. Restructure the pre-2007 logic so an unmarked ship may defer the marking only when a valid first scheduled dry-docking date after 1 July 2007 is evidenced and has not yet arrived; if the marking is already complete and equals the certificate maximum amidships draught, permit conformance without dry-docking-date evidence, while ensuring missing date evidence cannot make an unmarked ship pass accidentally."}
